{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:28f766cb2420df06","name":"Rebel Honor Guard","source":{"id":"source:reference-28f766cb2420df06","title":"Rebel Honor Guard","revision":20744,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:26:02Z","sha256":"aae502959701e99ccd7e276886875c8291d61548e110f883295b1e1a433e8740","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20744","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Rebel%20Honor%20Guard&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-28f766cb2420df06","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rebellion Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rebellion_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebel Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebel_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:52c543ff6d31425c"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The guerilla nature of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebel Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebel_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:52c543ff6d31425c"}," minimizes the use of ceremonial uniforms and personnel. However, there are occasions when pomp and formality are either required by protocol or desired by Alliance leaders and soldiers alike: medal ceremonies, formal visits to high-ranking officials, and bereavement traditions, to name a few.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The first Rebel Honor Guards are survivors of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Alderaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Alderaan","referenceId":"reference:c7a6b713a1619ee9"},", and they adapt their Alderaanian dress uniforms for their new role. Trained as bodyguards, they are the protectors of the Alliance leadership at formal occasions. Though Honor Guards are not trained to the same level of ability or fanaticism as ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Royal Guard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Royal_Guard?action=edit&redlink=1"},", they are professional, loyal protectors. Honor Guard personnel are regularly rotated back into standard Rebel units. There they share their new training with other unit members, which increases the likelihood that a few Honor Guards are available in any given sector.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["However, the primary reason for the personnel rotation is that ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mon Mothma"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mon_Mothma","referenceId":"reference:b0b5999c2a9f88e6"}," knows the dangers of keeping an elite unit too close to the Alliance's leadership. By rotating the troops, she hopes to prevent the Honor Guards from becoming too loyal to any single leader, and to prevent them from developing a sense of elitism.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Rebel Honor Guard Statistics (CL 5)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 6/",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +11; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +9\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w